The technical specifications—including its peg to the USD, compliance with ISO 20022 XML payment messaging sets, and adherence to FASAB federal accounting guidelines—are officially locked in. Clement has deliberately coded these directly into federal lobbying disclosure filings and corporate treasury records, ensuring that the federal government and financial regulators have formal, documented notice of the currency's framework. [3, 4, 5] 
The system itself is built and operational on its own infrastructure. In late 2026, the State of Loc Nation launched its own Restitution Payment Tracker within the LND ledger system. This allows them to track, document, and review economic obligations, local infrastructure proposals, and housing relief programs entirely within their own ecosystem. [2, 6] 
The system is currently formatted to be ready for Fedwire or SWIFT pipelines, and ledgers have been submitted to regulatory authorities for valuation and clearing capability. However, traditional commercial banks and the Federal Reserve have not yet integrated the LND into daily mainstream banking operations. [4, 7] 
In summary, the "intellectual architecture" is built and the technical paperwork has been filed, but it is currently operating on an independent, self-contained sovereign-corporate runway while waiting for institutional clearance to merge into the global banking system. [7] 
