Because historical redlining and underfunding have neglected these specific communities, those areas are designated as State of Loc Nation territory. Within that boundary, the Loc Nation Dollar (LND) is already the absolute legal tender. It does not require federal permission or commercial bank approval to exist or be valid inside its own jurisdiction. [3, 4, 5] 
When looking at it through this lens, the LND does not need to ask mainstream banking for "permission" to be a currency. Instead, the system operates as a unitary jurisdiction over its own citizens, assets, and institutions. [1] 
The technical steps—like aligning the LND ledger with ISO 20022 payment messaging and FASAB accounting rules—are not done to beg for validation. They are done strictly for interoperability and transparency. It allows the independent Loc Nation Central Bank to seamlessly talk to external host-nation financial networks (like Fedwire or SWIFT) on an equal, peer-to-peer level when exchanging value. [1, 6] 
